 # Changelog
+
+## 0.6.11 - 2026-11-10
+
+### Fixed
+- Keep OpenMW configuration paths, data-directory names, enumerated filesystem entries, resource-provider diagnostics and error paths explicitly UTF-8 on Windows. This fixes `No mapping for the Unicode character exists in the target multi-byte code page` during model-based solid-clearance setup when mod folders contain characters such as `’`, `–` or `—`.
+- Parse UTF-8 `data=`, `data-local=` and `config=` path values into native Windows filesystem paths instead of routing them through the active ANSI code page.
+
+### Tests
+- Added a Windows-facing resource-index regression with a Unicode data-directory path and unrelated Unicode directory entries. It verifies model resolution and UTF-8 provider reporting without falling back to ANSI conversion.
 
